course: dictionary
lesson: 13478
title: Hypothesis: a guess you can test
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hypothesis is an idea or guess that explains something, and that you can test. Scientists use the word a lot, but you can meet it in any subject. «Mia thinks plants grow faster in sunlight. That is her hypothesis.» Her idea is not proven yet, so she has to test it first.
explain: Context clues help you here. Words like test, experiment, results and supported show that a hypothesis is being checked. «We will test our hypothesis with two plants, one in the sun and one in the dark.» The test is what makes the guess useful.
explain: Hypothesis is a noun, and its plural is hypotheses. Check the meaning by swapping in the words idea or guess. If the sentence still makes sense, you have understood it. Remember that a hypothesis is not yet a fact.
fact: A hypothesis is an idea or guess that explains something and that you can test.
fact: In science, you form a hypothesis, then test it with an experiment or observation.
fact: «Hypothesis» can also mean any idea used as a starting point for thinking, which may or may not be true.
fact: «Hypotheses» is the plural: it means more than one hypothesis.
fact: «Test a hypothesis» means check whether the guess is right, using evidence.
exercise: «Mia thinks plants grow faster in sunlight. That is her hypothesis.» What is a hypothesis here? | *An idea or guess that can be tested | A type of sunlight | A kind of plant | A sure fact that nobody can change
exercise: «We will test our hypothesis with two plants, one in the sun and one in the dark.» What does test mean in this sentence? | Paint a picture of the plants | Read the book again | Eat and drink | *Check whether the idea is right, using an experiment
exercise: Which word is the plural of hypothesis? | hypothesise | *hypotheses | hypothesize | hypothetical
test: «The hypothesis was supported: the plant in the sun grew taller.» What does supported suggest? | The plant was made of paper | Nobody looked at the results | The hypothesis was wrong and must be thrown away | *The results agreed with the guess
test: The teacher says, «Let's start with a hypothesis about why the bridge cracked.» What does hypothesis mean here? | A tool for cutting paper | *A starting idea that may or may not be true | A proven fact | A test that has already finished
exam: Ravi says, «My hypothesis is that ice melts faster in warm water.» Why is this a hypothesis and not a proven fact? | It is always true | *It is a guess that still needs testing | It is written in a book | Ice never melts
